  "id": "foregroundbackground",
  "term": "foreground–background",
  "definition": "In image-based learning, foreground–background refers to the contrast between the target object or lesion and the surrounding image area. The packet supports this mainly in the sense that poor separation or imbalance between lesion and background can make detection harder, especially when boundaries are low in contrast and background samples greatly outnumber target samples.",
